1 CONTINUE
    The CONTINUE command resumes a command procedure that CTRL/Y (or
    CTRL/C) interrupted, and the image it was running, if one was (see
    HELP KEYS).  Anywhere else it does nothing, and leaves $STATUS as it
    was: in a command procedure, ON ERROR THEN CONTINUE makes the
    procedure go on after an error.

    Syntax:

        CONTINUE
